  "Question": "Ms. Hamilton’s eighth-grade class wants to participate in the annual three-person-team basketball tournament. Lance, Sally, Joy, and Fred are chosen for the team. In how many ways can the three starters be chosen?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(2\\)",
    "B": "\\(4\\)",
    "C": "\\(6\\)",
    "D": "\\(8\\)",
    "E": "\\(10\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Choosing three starters from four players leaves exactly one player out. That player can be Lance, Sally, Joy, or Fred, giving four choices.\n\nEvery group of three leaves out exactly one person, and different omitted players give different groups. Thus all starter groups are counted exactly once, for \\(\\boxed{4}\\) ways, choice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
